Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the *Software Engineer I* position with *Crusoe*. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience, a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, and hands-on experience building reliable distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, and user-facing APIs. The Cloud Network team's opportunity to learn network engineering while delivering high-performance infrastructure strongly matches both my foundation and growth goals.

At Sperse, I built and operated a production distributed-systems platform with Python, FastAPI, and Temporal that routes requests across 40+ services and agents for more than 10,000 users. I developed clean, well-tested, maintainable code for 160+ backend actions with validated contracts, access controls, and OpenTelemetry monitoring, then supported safe rollout through CI/CD gates for latency, accuracy, and safety. I also built a Git-based code review pipeline that automates triage across 25–30 pull requests each week. That work taught me to pair implementation with testing, design documentation, feedback, and architecture and design discussions—the engineering habits Crusoe expects as features progress from cloud systems to user-facing APIs.

At Qualitest, I engineered cloud infrastructure in Java and Spring Boot for a storage service spanning AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO. I also led testing and rollout with AWS Step Functions and Lambda, improving error recovery across more than 100,000 weekly executions. Outside work, I built an open source distributed-systems orchestrator that coordinates dependency-aware work across multiple machines with retries and timeout handling. These experiences give me a practical base in Java, distributed computing, source control, and reliable software operations while I deepen my knowledge of Linux fundamentals, cloud network primitives, and network engineering.

Crusoe's mission to accelerate the abundance of energy and intelligence is compelling because it connects infrastructure engineering to an energy-first future for AI. I would be excited to bring a collaborative mindset and growth mindset to a team that moves fast, makes things, and taps into collective genius. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration; I look forward to connecting.

